Dear Pharos Quality Team,

I am writing to report a critical quality incident involving our recent receipt of Insulin Glargine 100 IU/mL Injection (Product Code: INS-GLA-100), Batch Number: IG-26034-SG, Expiry: 05/2028.

Upon receiving the air freight shipment at our Singapore temperature-controlled hub this morning (27 July 2026), our QA team noted that the internal dataloggers recorded a temperature excursion. The pallets experienced temperatures reaching up to 18°C for approximately 6 hours during transit. 

Furthermore, upon visual inspection of 50 randomly sampled vials, 12 vials exhibited abnormal cloudiness and precipitation, which is highly uncharacteristic for this solution. 

We have quarantined the entire shipment of 8,500 vials. This product was scheduled for distribution to regional hospitals by tomorrow. Please urgently advise on the disposition of this batch, and whether you require samples to be sent back to your central laboratory for analysis. 

